## raylibx.pengu
## The facade of the `raylibx` layer: one module that imports all thirteen wrapper
## families, so the whole layer can be checked, built and reviewed as a unit.
##
## ## Why this module exists
## PenguScript has **no re-export**: `@export` names a C symbol and nothing makes an
## imported symbol visible through a second module. So this facade cannot give you
## `raylibx.split_text`; what it gives you is a single entry point that pulls the whole
## layer into one compilation:
##
##     pengu check --entry pengu/raylibx.pengu     # every family, at once
##     pengu build --entry pengu/raylibx.pengu     # and one bundle that links
##
## That matters because `pengu check` on a single family file **cannot** see a C symbol
## collision between two families — enchantings generate their C functions from the type
## and method names, so two families adding the same method to the same type would only
## fail when something imported both. This module is that something. It is the layer's
## integration test.
##
## ## How to use the layer
## Import the families you need, with an alias, and call through it:
##
## ```pengu
## import raylib
## import raylibx.text as text
## import raylibx.images as images
##
## weave main into int:
##     var img as raylib.Image is calling images.gen_image_color with 32, 32, raylib.RED
##     defer calling images.unload_image with img
##     var parts as list of string is calling text.split_text with "a,b", ","
##     defer banish parts
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## The fourteen families
## | Module | What it wraps |
## |---|---|
## | `raylibx.colors` | `Color` methods and the colour helpers |
## | `raylibx.files` | file, directory, path and clipboard-of-files functions |
## | `raylibx.shapes` | 2D shapes, with 20 `Vector2` and 7 `Rectangle` methods |
## | `raylibx.shapes3d` | 3D primitives, with 4 `Vector3` methods |
## | `raylibx.text` | fonts and text, with 5 `Font` methods |
## | `raylibx.input` | keyboard, mouse, gamepad, touch and gestures |
## | `raylibx.images` | the image pipeline, with 52 `Image` methods |
## | `raylibx.textures` | `Texture` and `RenderTexture` |
## | `raylibx.drawing` | the `Begin`/`End` frame-state pairs |
## | `raylibx.window` | window state, monitors and the clipboard |
## | `raylibx.shaders` | shader loading and typed uniforms |
## | `raylibx.models` | meshes, materials, models, animations and 3D collision |
## | `raylibx.audio` | waves, sounds, music and audio streams |
## | `raylibx.random` | randomness: `between` and `sequence`, plus the four measured traps |
##
## Every family's own plan is in `docs/wrappers/raylibx-<family>.md`, and the layer's shared
## decisions are in `docs/README.md`.

import raylibx.audio as audio
import raylibx.colors as colors
import raylibx.drawing as drawing
import raylibx.files as files
import raylibx.images as images
import raylibx.input as input
import raylibx.models as models
import raylibx.random as random
import raylibx.shaders as shaders
import raylibx.shapes as shapes
import raylibx.shapes3d as shapes3d
import raylibx.text as text
import raylibx.textures as textures
import raylibx.window as window

## This module has no weaves of its own: it exists so that the whole layer is compiled,
## type-checked and linked as one unit. Every symbol lives in the family that owns it.
weave main into int:
    return 0
